.TH HD-KERNEL 7 "October 2026" "hd-kernel" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-kernel \- the HyprDebian kernel with a prebuilt ZFS module
.SH DESCRIPTION
The package
.B hd-kernel
depends on the most recent HyprDebian kernel of the suite and its ZFS module,
so that they are installed and upgraded with it:
.TP
.BI linux-image- release
The kernel of Debian, with the patches and the config of Debian, built by the
build server of HyprDebian.
.TP
.BI zfs-modules- release
The ZFS module of the
.B zfs-linux
of Debian, built against that kernel, in
.IR /lib/modules/ release /extra/zfs .
It provides
.BR zfs-modules ,
which
.B zfs-initramfs
takes in place of
.BR zfs-dkms .
.PP
The release is
.IB x.y.z +debNN-hd id -amd64\fR,
such as
.BR 7.2.12+deb14-hd1a2b3c-amd64 ,
where
.I id
comes from the versions of
.BR linux ,
.B zfs-linux
and
.BR hd-kernel .
A new build has a new release, so it installs next to the kernel that runs.
.PP
Every build signs the modules of the kernel and the ZFS module with a key it
makes for the build and then throws away; the kernel trusts that key and no
other for its modules.
A system with this kernel needs neither DKMS nor a compiler for ZFS, and
under Secure Boot not even root can load a module that the build did not
sign.
.SH SWITCHING
To switch a system to the HyprDebian kernel:
.PP
.RS
sudo apt install hd-kernel
.RE
.PP
This removes
.BR linux-image-amd64 ,
.B linux-headers-amd64
and
.BR linux-base-amd64 ,
so the kernels of Debian get no more upgrades.
After the installation the bootloader shows the new kernel at the top of its
menu, with
.B -hd
in its name, see
.BR hd-bootloader-update (8).
Once it boots, the kernels of Debian can go:
.PP
.RS
sudo apt purge linux-image-<version>-amd64 linux-headers-<version>-amd64
.br
sudo apt autoremove --purge
.RE
.PP
The second command removes the packages that those two pulled in, such as
.BR linux-base- ,
.B linux-binary-
and
.B linux-modules-<version>-amd64
of the kernels of Debian since forky.
.PP
To switch back to the kernel of Debian, which gets its ZFS module from
.B zfs-dkms
again:
.PP
.RS
sudo apt install linux-image-amd64 linux-headers-amd64
.RE
.PP
This removes
.BR hd-kernel ;
the HyprDebian kernels stay until they are purged.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR /boot/vmlinuz- release
.TQ
.IR /lib/modules/ release
The kernel and its modules.
.TP
.IR /lib/modules/ release /extra/zfs
The ZFS module.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-bootloader-update (8),
.BR hd-buildserver (8),
.BR zfs (4)
